# <%= current_page.data.title %>

The CJS Common Platform (CPP) supports the criminal courts in England and Wales. It is a distinct platform with its own access, deployment and operational processes.

New joiners should read and follow the [onboarding](onboarding/index.html) process to obtain access.

If you are adding a service, start with [onboarding a service](onboarding/service.html), then follow the [new component](new-component/index.html) and [Path to Live](path-to-live/index.html) guides.

For an orientation to how the platform is put together, the language it uses and where
the authoritative documentation lives, start with [architecture](architecture/index.html).
It links the published [architecture model](https://hmcts.github.io/cp-c4-architecture/).

The [tools and configuration](tools-and-configuration/index.html) page explains where CPP service versions, deployment configuration and shared platform tooling live.

The [Helm charts](helm-charts/index.html) section catalogues the shared charts every CPP deployment uses, and how to use and customise them.

The [standards](standards/index.html) section covers shared platform services, starting with [CPP Artifactory](standards/artifactory/index.html) — where every CPP artefact is published and resolved from.
